    <briefdescription>
<para>PROPS and several other specifications from the RUNSPECS file record. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>R. Manasipov </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2014-2015</para>
</simplesect>
ASCII file interface to read corner point grid from ( *.GRDECL, *.grdecl ) file. In order to build a native CSMP <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_model" kindref="compound">Model</ref> the provided grid information is assigned to <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_v_set" kindref="compound">VSet</ref> and <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_model_topology" kindref="compound">ModelTopology</ref> objects. The regions that are constructed by default are: % regions which include all the cells MATRIX MATRIX_ACTIVE MATRIX_INACTIVE % and specific fault regions</para>
<para>In addition to grid information the properties such as: &apos;permeability&apos;, &apos;porosity&apos;, &apos;pressure&apos;, &apos;saturation&apos; can be readed as well. User is able to control property type and placement. For example one can create tensor or scalar permeability variables or to place &apos;pressure&apos; at the nodes or elements.</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">KEYWORDS<sp/>that<sp/>can<sp/>be<sp/>currently<sp/>handled:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">---<sp/>Grid</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">DIMENS</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">DX</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">DY</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">DZ</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">SPECGRID</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">TOPS</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">COORD</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ZCORN</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">FAULTS</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">---<sp/>Regions</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ACTNUM</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">SATNUM</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">PVTNUM</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">ROCKNUM</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EQLNUM</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">---<sp/>Props</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">NTG</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">PORO</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">PERMX<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">well.well_data_.push_back(<sp/>wellcomp<sp/>);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">PERMY</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">PERMZ</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">PRESSURE</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">SWAT</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">SOIL</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">SGAS</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">---<sp/>Runspec</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">WELSPECS</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">COMPDAT<sp/>(relies<sp/>on<sp/>WELLSPECS<sp/>and<sp/>can<sp/>therefore<sp/>not<sp/>be<sp/>defined<sp/>in<sp/>isolation)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
